{"name":"Black Coral","hex":"#54626f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black coral","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various tropical corals of the family Antipathidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_coral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black coral","blocks":[{"text":"Antipatharians, also known as black corals or thorn corals, are an order of soft deep-water corals. These corals can be recognized by their jet-black or dark brown chitin skeletons, which are surrounded by their colored polyps. Antipatharians are a cosmopolitan order, existing in nearly every oceanic location and depth, with the sole exception of brackish waters. However, they are most frequently found on continental slopes under 50 m (164 ft) deep. A black coral reproduces both sexually and asexually throughout its lifetime. Many black corals provide housing, shelter, food, and protection for other animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Blackcoral_colony_600.jpg/330px-Blackcoral_colony_600.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_coral"},{"title":"Coral","blocks":[{"text":"Corals are colonial marine invertebrates within the subphylum Anthozoa of the phylum Cnidaria. They typically form compact colonies of many identical individual polyps. Coral species include the important reef builders that inhabit tropical oceans and secrete calcium carbonate to form a hard skeleton."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg/330px-Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"},{"title":"Coral (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The various tones of the color coral are orange, red and pink representations of the colors of those cnidarians known as precious corals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Antipathes_sp_a_1520_m.jpg/500px-Antipathes_sp_a_1520_m.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Antipathes_sp_a_1520_m.jpg/500px-Antipathes_sp_a_1520_m.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntipathes_sp_a_1520_m.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Aphanipathes.jpg/500px-Aphanipathes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Aphanipathes.jpg/1280px-Aphanipathes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Aphanipathes.jpg/500px-Aphanipathes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAphanipathes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th